DESCRIPTION:Fibonacci Day falls on November 23 because the American way of 
 writing the date\, 11/23\, spells out 1\, 1\, 2\, 3 — the opening of the
  Fibonacci sequence. No founding body or proclamation designates the day\,
  and that arithmetic is the only explanation on offer. It suits a sequence
  older than the man it is named for\, and a man whose name is disputed.\n\
